       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because it would exceed the maximum daily dose of acetaminophen.\n\n- **Ordered:** 2000 mg \u00d7 3 per day = **6,000 mg/day**\n- **Standard adult maximum:** 4,000 mg/day. Many institutions use 3,000 mg/day. A single dose is usually capped at 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** 6 g/day could cause hepatotoxicity, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\n2000 mg may be a typo for 1000 mg, or the intended frequency may differ. These are some common options for a 70 kg adult with normal liver and kidney function:\n\n- 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum)\n- 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n\nTell me which dose you want, and confirm it with your supervising resident or attending if you're unsure. I'll enter it once you do."
